    "answer": {
      "short": "$N(t)=\\dfrac{1000}{1+24e^{-1000kt}}$, where $k=\\dfrac1{1000}\\ln\\!\\left(\\dfrac{48}{23}\\right)\\approx7.357\\times10^{-4}$. $N(5)\\approx623$ animals.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dt}{dN}&=\\frac1{kN(1000-N)}\\\\\\frac{dt}{dN}&=\\frac1{1000k}\\left(\\frac1N+\\frac1{1000-N}\\right)\\\\t&=\\frac1{1000k}\\left(\\ln|N|-\\ln|1000-N|\\right)+D\\\\\\ln\\left|\\frac{N}{1000-N}\\right|&=1000kt-1000kD\\\\\\frac{N}{1000-N}&=Ae^{1000kt}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe exponent is $1000kt$. Using $N(0)=40$,\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{40}{960}\\\\A&=\\frac1{24}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{N}{1000-N}&=\\frac1{24}e^{1000kt}\\\\24N&=(1000-N)e^{1000kt}\\\\N(24+e^{1000kt})&=1000e^{1000kt}\\\\N&=\\frac{1000}{1+24e^{-1000kt}}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $N(1)=80$,\n$$\\begin{align*}80&=\\frac{1000}{1+24e^{-1000k}}\\\\1+24e^{-1000k}&=12.5\\\\e^{-1000k}&=\\frac{11.5}{24}=\\frac{23}{48}\\\\k&=-\\frac1{1000}\\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{48}\\right)\\\\k&\\approx7.357\\times10^{-4}\\quad\\text{(4 significant figures)}.\\end{align*}$$\nRetaining the exact value of $k$,\n$$\\begin{align*}e^{-5000k}&=\\left(\\frac{23}{48}\\right)^5\\\\N(5)&=\\frac{1000}{1+24\\left(\\frac{23}{48}\\right)^5}\\\\N(5)&\\approx622.5721603.\\end{align*}$$\nThe population after 5 time units is approximately $623$ animals.",
